timeline
  title History of the web

  section Early web
    1989 : Tim Berners-Lee proposes the web at CERN
    1991 : First public web page goes live
    1993 : Mosaic browser released
    1994 : W3C founded by Tim Berners-Lee

  section Browser wars
    1995 : Netscape Navigator dominant
         : Internet Explorer launches
    1998 : Mozilla Foundation formed
    2003 : Safari released by Apple

  section Modern era
    2004 : Firefox 1.0 released
         : Web 2.0 term popularized
    2008 : Google Chrome released
    2015 : Microsoft Edge replaces IE
    2020 : Chromium-based Edge ships

  section Ambient web
    2022 : WebAssembly mainstream
    2024 : Browser-native AI APIs land
    2026 : Open standards for agent web
